    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras face a high-variance schedule today, headlined by the explosive speed-and-power profile of **Trea Turner** (78.26). Facing Sugano, **Trea Turner** benefits from a massive 18% SP skill boost and the lead-off spot, making him our primary engine for Runs and SBs. **Kyle Schwarber** (74.74) pairs perfectly with him in that same matchup, carrying an elite 0.395 xwOBA into a favorable park environment. While **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28) draws a tougher southpaw matchup against Abbott, his elite profile keeps his floor well above the rest of the roster. Notably, **Dillon Dingler** (60.86) and **Junior Caminero** (63.50) secure strong starts; **Dillon Dingler** leverages a dynamic platoon edge against the lefty Cameron, while **Junior Caminero** maintains a high utility score despite a modest SP matchup, thanks to aggressive placement at the top of the order.\n\nThe margin for error remains razor-thin for the bottom of our lineup. **Caleb Durbin** (59.99) is starting primarily for his elite sprint speed and category scarcity, as his batting order position (#9) significantly handicaps his base projection. The most difficult bench decision involved **Chase Meidroth** (37.95); he fell just short of our 40.0 floor due to a brutal draw against Logan Gilbert. While he typically offers value, the risk of a sub-40 performance necessitated his removal to preserve our limited game caps. We are also monitoring **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (52.12) closely; while his dynamic platoon advantage is clear, he faces the elite arm of deGrom, which introduces high volatility for his SB-heavy profile. We continue to hold **Zac Veen**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Lars Nootbaar** in reserve as we await roster flexibility; their absence, combined with the active benching of **Chase Meidroth**, leaves us focused on maximizing the efficiency of our current starters to avoid burning unproductive at-bats.",
